Guidelime.registerGuide([[
[N 30-31 Razorfen Kraul]
[D Forever Alliance 1-30 (Braedyn)\\The optional last trip: Razorfen Kraul in the far south of the Barrens (Blueleaf Tubers, Willix the Importer, Mortality Wanes and, for the shaman, Elemental Aid), the way there by boat, bird and the Barrens road, boss notes, loot calls and the hearth home.]
[GA Alliance]
[OC]|cffffffffLevel 30|r  -  you start in Stormwind with chapter 25's loose ends done; hearth = Sentinel Hill and it stays there. This is the last chapter of the 1-30 guide and it is optional: one dungeon, Razorfen Kraul (mobs 24-33, bosses 28-33) in the far south of the Barrens, about 8,200 quest XP (about 10,850 for the shaman) plus a full clear and the best level 29-31 leather and two-handers on the route. 5,150 of that XP is certain; the other 3,050 (Mortality Wanes) hangs on a drop. The trip is long (boat, bird, then a ride through Horde country): do it when you have an hour and a half free
[OC]|cffffcc00Group content:|r Forever caps the instance at 5 players. Bring the tank friend and a healer; you two are the damage. Entry level is 25 (a Forever write-up says the Group Finder lists it from 24)
[OC]|cffffcc00Sources:|r quest ids, levels, drops and item stats come from the Forever DB (boss levels are the Classic values; boss HP is not in the DB). Boss tactics, the layout, the escort and the gopher are Classic-era guide knowledge (Icy Veins, warcraft.wiki.gg) plus two Forever write-ups (Warcraft Tavern, kami-labs); none of it is verified on Forever
[OC]|cffffcc00Supplies:|r nothing inside sells anything: food and water for 90 minutes, repair, empty bags, and (hunter) 400+ ammo bought before the boat - Astranaar sells none and the rest of the way is Horde country
[O][A Hunter] Train your level 30 spells if you have not: [TAR5515 Einris Brightspear] in the Dwarven District [T] [G67.3,36.2 Stormwind City]
[OC][A Shaman] No shaman trainer on this trip: your level 32 spells wait for Ironforge's Forlorn Cavern

[OC]|cffffffffRazorfen Kraul|r  -  |cFFFF0000GROUP 5|r, entry level 25, mobs 24-33, bosses 28-33 plus two rares, ~60 min. Blueleaf Tubers starts in Ratchet on the way, Willix and Mortality Wanes inside, and Elemental Aid is already in the shaman's log:
[OC]|cffffcc00?|r Blueleaf Tubers (1221, needs level 20) - 6 Blueleaf Tubers - |cff66ff66normal|r: a Snufflenose Gopher digs them up for you in the Kraul's trench (gophers spawn nowhere else), so the cost is guarding the gopher. 2,100 XP + A Small Container of Gems at Mebok in Ratchet
[OC]|cffffcc00?|r Willix the Importer (1144, needs level 23) - escort Willix out of the Kraul - |cff66ff66normal|r, but it is an |cFFFF0000escort: everyone in the group must be on the quest before you talk to Willix|r (a Forever write-up says it cannot be shared, so each of you takes it from him). Willix is a level 27 elite in the DB. 3,050 XP + a ring
[OC]|cffffcc00?|r Mortality Wanes (1142, needs level 25) - Treshala's Pendant - |cFFFF0000luck, do not farm it|r: the DB lists the pendant on every quilboar type in the Kraul (27 of them, bosses included) but not the rate (a Forever write-up quotes about 0.7% a kill from Classic data), and Heralath, who gives the quest, lies near Charlga at the very end, so only the last pulls can drop it. Shareable: one of you takes it and shares it. 3,050 XP + Lancer Boots at Treshala in Darnassus, a separate trip. Take it because it is free, nothing more
[OC][A Shaman] |cffffcc00?|r Elemental Aid (96264, level 30) - defeat Charlga Razorflank and take the information from her (the DB gives her a Tattered Note as the objective item) - |cff66ff66normal|r: she is the last boss and the only source. 2,650 XP at Veyric Thunderhame in Arathi
[OC]|cffffcc00Not for you:|r The Crone of the Kraul (1101: Lonebrow's Journal at the Great Lift in Thousand Needles, then Falfindel Waywarder in Feralas, far off this route), the Horde quests off Charlga and the Kraul Bats, and the warrior quests for Roogug's Vial of Phlogiston

[OC]|cffffffffThe way there|r  -  Stormwind harbor boat to Auberdine (~5 min), the flight to Astranaar, then a ride of 15 minutes or so: the road east out of Ashenvale past Splintertree Post, through the Mor'shan Rampart on the border, past the Crossroads and on east to Ratchet, the neutral goblin port with the quest giver. Horde guards (level 40 in the DB) stand at Splintertree Post, the Rampart, the Crossroads and Camp Taurajo: stay on the road and never stop in their yards
[OC][A Shaman] Ghost Wolf for the whole ride (outdoors only); drop it before Ratchet's crowd so you can talk
[OC][A Hunter] Aspect of the Cheetah for the ride; swap to Hawk at the entrance
Walk down to the harbor; the Auberdine boat leaves from the northern pier [G24.5,4 Stormwind City]
Ride the boat to Auberdine. At flight master [TAR3841 Caylais Moonfeather], |cFFfff8a3Fly to [F Astranaar]|r [G36.3,45.6 Darkshore]
[OC]Classic-era route, unverified on Forever: from Astranaar the road runs east to Splintertree Post (the Horde fort at 73,61 in Ashenvale) and leaves it southward; the Mor'shan Rampart is the Horde gate on the border at the north end of the Barrens road. The Ashenvale marker below is the road just south of the fort, taken from the TUGs Horde guide
Ride east out of Astranaar on the main road, past Splintertree Post and out of Ashenvale on its southern road [G71,68.4 Ashenvale]
Follow the road through the Mor'shan Rampart and into the Barrens [G46.7,8.4 The Barrens]
Keep to the road south toward the Crossroads but pass it on the east side (Horde town, guards), then ride on east along the road to Ratchet [G56.0,35.6 The Barrens]

[OC]|cffffffffRatchet|r  -  neutral and safe for both of you. Take the flight path, the quest and the three things beside Mebok, then ride south
At flight master [TAR16227 Bragok], get the [P Ratchet] flight path (free; the way home is the hearth) [G63.1,37.2 The Barrens]
At [TAR3446 Mebok Mizzyrix], [QA1221 Blueleaf Tubers] (hand-in here again after the Kraul) [G62.4,37.6 The Barrens]
Next to him pick up the Crate with Holes and the Snufflenose Command Stick and read the Snufflenose Owner's Manual (all three are objects at his stand, nothing is bought) [G62.3,37.6 The Barrens]
[OC]|cffffcc00The gopher (Classic-era):|r inside the Kraul, use the Crate with Holes to summon a Snufflenose Gopher (a crate holds up to five; one is enough). Use the Command Stick on the gopher to start it digging or recall it; the way you face roughly aims it. It smells a tuber from fifty paces and leaves a lootable Blueleaf Tuber on the ground. It draws aggro like a combat pet but does not fight, and it despawns if it dies, if you die or if you leave: recall it near packs. It only works in the trench behind Charlga's hut, so do the tubers there. Keep the Crate and the Stick: Mebok wants both back with the 6 tubers
Ride back west to the main road and follow it south to Camp Taurajo (Horde camp, guards: stay on the road) [G44.5,59.2 The Barrens]
[OC]|cffffcc00If you wipe (Classic-era):|r the nearest graveyard is Camp Taurajo, 30 units north of the entrance: release, take the Spirit Healer there and ghost back down the road. The Hearthstone works inside, so there is no walk out
|cFFFF0000GROUP 5|r Keep following the road south to the bottom of the Barrens and meet the group at the Kraul, a mass of giant thorns on the west side; enter Razorfen Kraul [G42.9,90.2 The Barrens]
[OC][A Hunter] |cffffcc00In a group:|r pet on passive, Growl OFF, send it only at the tank's target. Freezing Trap is your one crowd control

[OC]|cffffffffThe run|r  -  Icy Veins' route (Classic-era): stay on the top level and do not drop into the trench until Charlga is dead. Order: Roogug (optional), Aggem Thorncurse, Death Speaker Jargba, Overlord Ramtusk, Agathelos, Charlga, with Earthcaller Halmgar and the Blind Hunter as rares that may not show. Trash is all quilboar: warriors, quilguards, wardens, defenders and spearhides (24-30), shaman casters (geomancers, dustweavers, groundshakers, earthbreakers, totemics; 25-31), Death's Head cultists (acolyte, adept, priest, sage, seer; 26-30) and handlers, beast trainers and beastmasters (25-31). One pack at a time, casters first
[OC]Razorfen Dustweavers (28-29) cast Enveloping Winds, a crowd control that snowballs into a wipe: if it lands on the healer, the tank stops pulling and whoever can heal helps. The Kraul Bats past Ramtusk (30-32) silence. Shaman: Earth Shock the casters (interrupts), Poison Cleansing Totem if you have the Water Totem
[OC]|cffffcc00Roogug|r (28 elite, optional - only the warrior quests want his Vial of Phlogiston): Lightning Bolt and a summoned Earth Rumbler, no mechanics. He is the first boss and a short detour; hunter: he is one of five bosses that can drop Brawler's Leather Helm, shaman: nothing for you
[OC]|cffffcc00Aggem Thorncurse|r (30 elite): Chain Heal and a summoned Boar Spirit; interrupt the heals and kill the spirit first. Icy Veins lists no other mechanics
[OC]|cffffcc00Loot (Aggem, both):|r |cff66ff66Thorncursed Grips|r (leather gloves +18 attack power, req 27; each melee hit also deals 2 Nature damage to you and the target, harmless) are the gloves to take - a Forever beta survey rates the drop about 2%, so do not count on them. Thornspike is a dagger - pass
[OC]|cffffcc00Death Speaker Jargba|r (30 elite) and his cultists: Shadow Bolt and Dominate Mind. Pulling one pulls the pack, so crowd-control what you can (hunter: Freezing Trap on a caster) and kill them one at a time. A Dominated player turns on the group for a few seconds: back off, do not hit them, the tank holds (a mage would Polymorph them)
[OC]|cffffcc00Loot (Jargba):|r Death Speaker Mantle, Robes and Scepter are cloth and a healing mace - pass; Stormrider's Leather Helm (Spirit) is not for you
[OC]|cffffcc00Overlord Ramtusk|r (32 elite): Battle Shout and Thunderclap, no mechanics; crowd-control his adds. Razorfen Spearhides (29-30 rare elites) may stand with him and have a high chance to drop Armor Piercer (Icy Veins)
[OC][A Shaman] |cffffcc00Loot (Ramtusk):|r |cff66ff66Corpsemaker|r (2H axe 28.95 dps +15 Str +8 Sta, req 29) - ROLL, the best two-hander on the route, 5 to 6 dps over Slaghammer or Reef Axe. Tusken Helm is mail - pass
[OC][A Hunter] |cffffcc00Loot (Ramtusk):|r nothing for you (a Str two-hander and a mail helm) - pass. |cff66ff66Armor Piercer|r from a Spearhide (2H polearm 19.81 dps +11 Agi, req 24) is a stat stick only if you trained Polearms (Woo Ping in Stormwind, chapter 08)
[OC]|cffffcc00Earthcaller Halmgar|r (32 rare elite, may not spawn; Icy Veins puts him on the platforms after Ramtusk): Earthbind Totem (kill it), Lightning Bolt and a summoned Earth Rumbler
[OC][A Shaman] |cffffcc00Loot (Halmgar):|r Wind Spirit Staff (21.4 dps +16 Spi, +23 spell damage, req 29) only if you have no better two-hander; Whisperwind Headdress is a caster helm - pass
[OC]|cffffcc00Agathelos the Raging|r (33 elite beast): Enrage, Rampage, Left for Dead and a Rushing Charge; no mechanics beyond that, the tank and healer ride out the enrage
[OC]|cffffcc00Loot (Agathelos, both):|r |cff66ff66Ferine Leggings|r (leather legs +12 Int, +26 attack power, req 29) - ROLL: the biggest upgrade of the run over Duty Bound Leggings or any Agility legs you carry (a Forever beta survey puts the drop near 56%). Swinetusk Shank is a caster dagger and the Quilrager Throwing Axe a thrown weapon - pass
[OC]|cffffcc00Blind Hunter|r (32 rare elite beast, may not spawn; Icy Veins: after Agathelos): Sonic Burst is an AoE silence, so casters and the healer stand at range; Ravage on the tank
[OC][A Hunter] |cffffcc00Loot (Blind Hunter):|r |cff66ff66Nightstalker Bow|r (bow 17.06 dps +3 Agi, +5 Shadow resistance, req 29) - ROLL, it beats Blackfathom's Naga Heartpiercer (13.3) and Fallenroot Longbow (13.9). Stygian Bone Amulet (neck +4 Sta, +5 spell damage) only for an empty neck slot; Batwing Mantle is cloth
[OC][A Shaman] |cffffcc00Loot (Blind Hunter):|r nothing for you: Stygian Bone Amulet (neck +4 Sta, +5 spell damage) only for an empty neck slot; Nightstalker Bow and the cloth Batwing Mantle - pass
[OC]|cffffcc00Charlga Razorflank|r (33 elite, last boss): Chain Bolt, Mana Spike, Purity and Renew (Classic-era). Interrupt her as often as you can (shaman: Earth Shock) and burn her down; the healer's mana and a spread-out group are what decide it
[A Shaman] Kill Charlga Razorflank and loot the Tattered Note [QC96264] - one kill only: Wowhead Forever shows the Note at under 1%, almost certainly because nearly every logged kill is a non-shaman; if it is not in her loot, do not re-run for it - abandon the quest
[OC]|cffffcc00Loot (Charlga):|r Heart of Agamaggan is a shield and Pronged Reaver a one-hand axe (22.9 dps +5 Str +5 Spi, unique) - pass both (the plan is a two-hander). Agamaggan's Clutch (ring +5 Sta +6 Spi, req 30) only for an empty ring slot
[OC][A Shaman] |cffffcc00Leather helms (req 25, bind on pickup):|r Charlga, Agathelos, Aggem and Halmgar drop |cff66ff66Defender's Leather Helm|r (+12 Str +13 Sta) - the call; skip it if you already won one in Blackfathom. Totemic (+13 Sta +12 spell damage; Charlga, Aggem) is second; Stormrider's is not for you
[OC][A Hunter] |cffffcc00Leather helms (req 25, bind on pickup):|r Roogug, Aggem, Jargba, Agathelos and Charlga can drop |cff66ff66Brawler's Leather Helm|r (+10 Agi +13 Sta) - the call; skip it if you already won one in the Stockade or Blackfathom. Whisperwind and Geomancer headdresses are caster helms - pass
[OC][A Shaman] |cffffcc00Trash loot:|r |cff66ff66Slaghammer|r (2H mace 23.75 dps +11 Str +10 Sta, req 24, bind on equip; 20 quilboar types drop it) is the stop-gap until Corpsemaker and already beats Reef Axe (22.4 dps +8 Str). |cff66ff66Mantle of Thieves|r (shoulders +10 Agi +4 Sta +3 Spi, req 25, bind on equip) if your shoulders are weaker. Wolfclaw Gloves (+5 Str +6 Agi +6 Sta) only for bare hands, Plains Ring (+8 Sta +3 Int) for an empty ring slot. Pysan's Old Greatsword is a sword - pass
[OC][A Hunter] |cffffcc00Trash loot:|r |cff66ff66Mantle of Thieves|r (shoulders +10 Agi +4 Sta +3 Spi, req 25, bind on equip; 19 quilboar types drop it) is your shoulder call. Wolfclaw Gloves (+5 Str +6 Agi +6 Sta) only for bare hands, Plains Ring (+8 Sta +3 Int) for an empty ring slot. Slaghammer is a Str mace - pass

[OC]|cffffffffCharlga's hut and the trench|r  -  after Charlga, jump down off the ledge behind her hut (Icy Veins): the trench holds Willix, the gopher's only hunting ground and the way out. Heralath Fallowbrook lies somewhere near Charlga (Warcraft Tavern; the DB has no coordinates for him or for Willix), so look round the hut first. Everyone takes each quest before the group moves on
At [TAR4510 Heralath Fallowbrook] near Charlga's hut, [QA1142 Mortality Wanes] (shareable: one of you takes it and shares it)
[OC]Treshala's Pendant is a quest-item drop: from here every quilboar can drop it, so kill what the trench and Willix's ambushes throw at you and check your bags at the exit. No pendant by then: forget it, do not clear again [QC1142]
[OC]|cffffcc00Tubers first:|r summon the gopher at the head of the trench, before you wake Willix, and let it work while the group holds the ground; the tank keeps the pack away from it
At the head of the trench, use the Crate with Holes, send the gopher out with the Command Stick and click each Blueleaf Tuber it digs up until you hold 6 [QC1221]
[OC]|cFFFF0000ESCORT:|r everyone in the group must be on the quest before you talk to Willix, then he walks the trench to the exit with quilboar ambushes on the way (Classic-era). Stay close to him: if you stray too far the quest fails. Recall the gopher first
At [TAR4508 Willix the Importer], [QA1144 Willix the Importer] (3,050 XP; all of you, together)
Walk Willix out of the Kraul [QC1144]
[OC]Willix finishes at the exit; a Forever write-up says to turn it in just outside the portal, so step out and look for him there before you decide he has gone
Hand in to [TAR4508 Willix the Importer] at the exit [QT1144] [G42.9,90.2 The Barrens]
[OC][A Hunter] |cffffcc00Gear (Willix):|r |cff66ff66Monkey Ring|r (+5 Agi +5 Spi). Tiger Band (+5 Str +5 Spi) and the new Boar Signet (+5 Sta, block) are not for you
[OC][A Shaman] |cffffcc00Gear (Willix):|r |cff66ff66Snake Hoop|r (+5 Int, +6 spell damage). Tiger Band (+5 Str +5 Spi) is a dead heat on this guide's stat weights - take whichever you prefer; Boar Signet is a shield ring - pass
[OC]|cffffcc00Gear (Mortality Wanes, if it ever drops):|r |cff66ff66Lancer Boots|r (leather +5 Agi +6 Sta +4 Spi) for both of you. Mourning Shawl (cloak +8 Sta, -4 Spi) and the new Sentinel's Boots (mail) are not for you

[OC]|cffffffffHome|r  -  Mebok first, then the hearth. The shaman then closes Elemental Aid in Arathi
Ride back north to Ratchet: the road past Camp Taurajo and the Crossroads, the same way you came [G62.4,37.6 The Barrens]
At [TAR3446 Mebok Mizzyrix], [QT1221] (give back the Crate with Holes and the Command Stick with the 6 tubers) [G62.4,37.6 The Barrens]
|cFFfff8a3Hearth to [H Sentinel Hill]|r
[A Shaman] At [TAR523 Thor], |cFFfff8a3Fly to [F Refuge Pointe]|r (a multi-hop flight through Stormwind, Ironforge and Menethil; the game routes it) [G56.5,52.6 Westfall]
[OC][A Shaman] Run about 24 map units north-east from Refuge Pointe and approach Veyric from the WEST: Highland Striders and Plains Creepers (30-33) on the way, and Fozruk (42 elite), the Cresting Exiles (38-39) and Myzrael (44 elite) stand east of him at about 63-68, 28-34. Stay in Ghost Wolf and do not go past him
[A Shaman] At [TAR259023 Veyric Thunderhame], [QT96264] (2,650 XP) [G59.8,27.6 Arathi Highlands]
[OC][A Shaman] |cffffcc00Veyric's other quests:|r The Tempest's Weapons (96016) and Heed My Call (96135) are level-40 content built around the Eye of the Tempest in Thousand Needles - leave them. At Refuge Pointe, |cFFfff8a3Fly to [F Stormwind]|r whenever you are done
[O]At [TAR4521 Treshala Fallowbrook] on the Tradesmen's Terrace, [QT1142] (3,050 XP + Lancer Boots; only if the Pendant dropped - Darnassus is the Auberdine boat, the Rut'theran boat and the portal, as in chapter 20, so do it on a later visit) [G69.5,67.8 Darnassus]
[OC]|cffffcc00Check:|r log should hold nothing from this chapter except, if the Pendant dropped, Mortality Wanes (1142) for a later Darnassus visit; if no Pendant dropped you may abandon it. Shaman: Elemental Aid (96264) is handed in; 96016 and 96135 stay in Veyric's list, untaken. Still open from chapter 25 on purpose: The Missing Diplomat 1248 (Menethil)
[OC]|cffffffffEnd of the 1-30 guide|r  -  that was the last chapter. From here the open pointers are the ones chapter 25 listed (the Refuge Pointe hub, the City of Dalaran dungeon, Scarlet Monastery), the three Dalaran lead-ins you carry into the 30-40 guide (A Green Sample 92456, Power Overwhelming 92489, An Alarming Request 92432 - Modera on the Silverpine shore 68.6,45.2 takes 92432 and gives Starving Arcane and Heart of Disruption), plus the Dustwallow end of the Missing Diplomat chain and Ratchet's boat to Booty Bay, which now has its flight path. Level 31-32 is the turn into the next guide
]], "Forever Alliance 1-30")
